From 08a292d0212dcc71a048a96485d4684e9d07e079 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:00:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] media: i2c: Add GalaxyCore GC5035 image sensor driver

Add a driver for the GalaxyCore GC5035, the colour filter camera of the
OnePlus 8 Pro, which also sees near infrared. It uses two D-PHY lanes and
a 19.2 MHz clock. The register settings come from the camera module data
of the phone.

The analogue gain control is an index into the gain table of the sensor,
and only the full resolution mode is supported.

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig  |  10 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile |   1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/gc5035.c | 948 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 959 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/gc5035.c

